  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical conducting spheres $P$ and $S$ with charge $Q$ on each, repel each other with a force $16 \\mathrm{~N}$. A third identical uncharged conducting sphere $R$ is successively brought in contact with the two spheres. The new force of repulsion between $\\mathrm{P}$ and $\\mathrm{S}$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "js0TA",
      "text": "$1 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4L89j",
      "text": "$6 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mB2xU",
      "text": "$12 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JQUQt",
      "text": "$4 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/BKDoEzkhtsftiaf7JdbQNNJd4EbmiiNtMZGOscSXc0A.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned}\n& F_{P S} \\propto Q^2 \\\\\n& F_{P S}=16 \\mathrm{~N}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Now If $\\mathrm{P} ~\\&~ \\mathrm{R}$ are brought in contact then\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/NTrtGxSR2AwUl33HCr9v-wS2DzdpLNck7AoucIw-k6M.original.fullsize.png\"><br />Now If $S \\& R$ are brought in contact then\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/GRQyVjbW1ZFBwv9o1lRPD9ci5RAJNiUjGxdMSQnWZh4.original.fullsize.png\"><br />New force between $P ~\\&~ S$ is :\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{PS}} \\propto \\frac{\\mathrm{Q}}{2} \\times \\frac{3 \\mathrm{Q}}{4} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~F}_{\\mathrm{PS}} \\propto \\frac{3 \\mathrm{Q}^2}{8}=\\frac{3}{8} \\times 16=6 \\mathrm{~N}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
